  {"clause_id": "c058", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Reliance on counsel is made \"subject to the provisions of Article Seven,\" but Article Seven concerns expenses of the Trust; the liability provisions are in Article Eight. The qualification on the Trustee's protection therefore cites the wrong article, and the clause also protects the Trustee both for following and \"for failing to follow\" the advice.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.28}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c059", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c060", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Clause (i) permits a sale of substantially all assets \"to another Series\" for consideration that \"may include Shares of or interests in such Series, entity, or series thereof,\" the later language presupposing a transferee entity the clause never authorizes. The class of permitted transferees cannot be read off the text, and the perpetual-existence sentence is immediately undone by the dissolution power that follows.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c061", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Making the Trustee's own \"best interests\" determination \"conclusive and binding\" sits against Section 3.3's prudent-person standard and Section 8.5's preservation of ERISA duties, which contemplate review of the Trustee's judgment. Whether the dissolution decision is truly unreviewable is left to construction.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.12}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c062", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Discharge of \"the Trustee and the Trust ... of any and all further liabilities and duties\" on termination cannot be squared with Section 8.3's indemnity to former Shareholders and Section 8.2's indemnification of Covered Persons, which contemplate obligations surviving winding up. Whether termination extinguishes accrued claims is unresolved.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.18}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c063", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c064", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The second paragraph refers to a merger agreement \"approved by the Trustees in accordance with this Section 4,\" but there is no Section 4 of Article Nine; the section is 9.4. The mis-citation leaves the approval requirement pointing at nothing.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.18}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c065", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c066", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The choice of \"the Maryland Act and the applicable laws of the State of Maryland\" cannot be squared with the Securities Lending Agreement, Section 12 of which chooses Minnesota law, or with Section 9(a) of the Subscription Agreement, which does the same for the same investment relationship. Which law governs a Shareholder's claim against the Trustee is a live question.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.33}
